{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-33627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the unit tangent vector to the curve\n $r(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (0,\\infty )?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),\\,y(t),\\,z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,1,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})}^{2}+(1)^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}+1+\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1+{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}}{{t}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+{t}^{2})^{2}}{{t}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{t}^{2}}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Finally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,1,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{t}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-33627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{1+t}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{1+t}⟨1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}t⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-74893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+(t+\\frac{4}{t})\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-74893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+\\frac{4}{t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{t}\\,i+(1-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}})\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{4}{t})}^{2}+{(1-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{{t}^{2}}+{(1-\\frac{8}{{t}^{2}}+\\frac{16}{{t}^{4}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{8}{{t}^{2}}+\\frac{16}{{t}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}({t}^{4}+8{t}^{2}+16)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}{({t}^{2}+4)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+4)}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{({t}^{2}+4)}(\\frac{4}{t}\\,i+(1-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}})\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+4)}(4t\\,i+({t}^{2}-4)\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-74893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-74893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-74893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{(\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1})}(t\\,i+(2{t}^{2}-4)\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+4)}(4t\\,i+({t}^{2}-4)\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+4)}(4t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+({t}^{2}-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}})\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}-4)}(4t\\,i+({t}^{2}+4)\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+4)}({t}^{2}\\,i+(2t-4)\\,j)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-74893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+4)}(4t\\,i+({t}^{2}-4)\\,j)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-74891" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-74891" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡2t+4{cos}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡2t+{cos}^{2}⁡2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-74891" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-74891" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-74891" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j"] ["math" "2(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j)"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-74891" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),\\,y(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-127212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "9⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\sqrt{t}\\,i+(2-t)\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i-\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}})}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4t}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1+4t}{4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1+4t}}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}i-\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{1+4t}(3i+2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{1+4t}(i-\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(\\sqrt{t}\\,i-2t\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-\\,j)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩$ at the point $P(1,1,4)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(1,1,4)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,4⟩ \\\\ ⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{t}^{4}=1 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ 4t=4.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, we get $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(1,1,4)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$  \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,2t,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨4(1)^{3},\\,2(1),\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(1,1,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨4,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =⟨\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4},\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-127221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},2⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4},-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},4⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{1}{4}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4},\\frac{1}{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4},\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}⟩$ at the point where $t=\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\pi :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\pi ,\\,0,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\pi )^{2}+(0)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}\\pi )^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\pi ) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\pi )}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }⟨-\\pi ,\\,0,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{7}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{7}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{12}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{12}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{12}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{12}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=2t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k$ at the point $P(2,1,1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,j+y(t)\\,j+z(t)\\,k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,1,1)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k \\\\ 2t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k & =2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2t=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ t=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(2,1,1)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2t\\,j+\\,k \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =2\\,i+2(1)\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(2,1,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩$ at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖ & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-33581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=(t+{t}^{3})p(t)$ at the point where $t=1$, if $p(1)=\\,i-2\\,j+k$ and ${p}^{′}(1)=-2\\,i+\\,j+2\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+{t}^{3})p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+{t}^{3})p(t)+(t+{t}^{3})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =(1+3{t}^{2})p(t)+(t+{t}^{3}){p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =(1+3(1)^{2})p(1)+(1+{1}^{3}){p}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =4(i-2\\,j+k)+2(-2\\,i+\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =-6j+8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(-6\\,j+8\\,k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=1$ is $T(1)=-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-127297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{10}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{10}\\,i-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{10}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{10}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{10}\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\,p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=0$, given that  $p(0)=2\\,i+j-k\\,$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(0)=i-2\\,j-2\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\,p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1})\\cdot p(t)+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2t}{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}}\\,p(t)+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{2(0)}{{({0}^{2}+1)}^{2}}\\,p(0)+\\frac{1}{{0}^{2}+1}\\,{p}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =0(2\\,i+j-k)+(\\,i-2\\,j-2k) \\\\  & =\\,i-2\\,j-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(0):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(0):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(0)}{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (i-2\\,j-2\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{2}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=0$ is  $T(0)=\\frac{1}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{2}{3}\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-127298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{2}{3}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{1}{3}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{2}{3}\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-75141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)={t}^{3}p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=1$, given that  $p(1)=-2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k\\,$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(1)=3\\,i-3\\,j+\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-75141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\cdot p(t)+{t}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,p(t)+{t}^{3}\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{2}\\,p(1)+(1)^{3}\\,{p}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =3(-2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k)+(3\\,i-3\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =-6\\,i+3\\,j+3k+3\\,i-3\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =-3\\,i+4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-3\\,i+4\\,k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=1$ is  $T(1)=-\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-75141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-75141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-75141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,j"] ["math" "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{5}\\,i+\\frac{1}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-75141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)={e}^{-t}p(t)$ at the point where $t=0$, if $p(0)=\\,i+\\,j+k$ and ${p}^{′}(0)=\\,i-\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})p(t)+{e}^{-t}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-t}p(t)+{e}^{-t}{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =-{e}^{0}p(0)+{e}^{0}{p}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =-(\\,i+\\,j+k)+(\\,i-\\,j) \\\\  & =-2j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(0)}{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}(-2j-k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=0$ is $T(0)=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}i-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"] ["math" "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"] ["math" "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}i-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$, given that  $p(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\sqrt{3}\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\,k$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=-2\\,i-8\\,j+4\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\cdot p(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,p(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})p(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3}){p}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3}\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\,k)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2\\,i-8\\,j+4\\,k) \\\\  & =(3\\,i+3\\,k)+(-\\,i-4\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\,i-4\\,j+5\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})‖ & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{‖{r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot (2\\,i-4\\,j+5\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,i-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is\n $T(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,i-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a"} {"question" "q-127280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,i-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,i-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\,i-\\frac{4}{15}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "q-127280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,i-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7853a132681843029de6668e2560b85e30c82dcfcf3d0f8a1770db1782a18fca"} {"question" "e-3055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle \\sin^3{t}, \\:\\cos^3{t} \\right\\rangle$ at an arbitrary point where $0 < t < \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/example-3055.json" "file_sha256" "3561411f6f0388be3be00ef7cde3f26299aa392c64661f5e493e98c9da61af02"} {"question" "e-3055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $\\mathbf r(t)= x(t) \\,\\mathbf i + y(t) \\,\\mathbf j,$ the unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(t)=\\dfrac{\\mathbf r'(t)}{\\left\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\right\\|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({sin}^{3}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({cos}^{3}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3{cos}^{2}⁡t(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf r'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\ \\text{ } & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the last step, we were able to remove the absolute value bars because $\\sin{t}>0$ and $\\cos{t}>0$ for $0 < t < \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we normalize $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/example-3055.json" "file_sha256" "3561411f6f0388be3be00ef7cde3f26299aa392c64661f5e493e98c9da61af02"} {"question" "e-3054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/1a5a0925f4e15e00c9eff4bb4f39ce9c6eda232881bbddb07184ac54bbc269a8.png) at the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/1e24125540d8b43cf8d314684fef6fb5be15c62d6988f9aac984f9812e6a74fd.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/example-3054.json" "file_sha256" "68229a275409fac4a8c441245885181942605d93d5ef27b8ba79c4762449d1ed"} {"question" "e-3054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/d7ec57597ee1ec3ed5d675c6d1cfde0115309f037e92d4aae963be1e54c97173.png) the unit tangent vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/beaa6501c934b5c7325c3b3385bae9fcc0388a74d5983995c83f4d8813e93f06.png) at the po